## Decision rule and review

Any exactness, pin, count, resource, failure-retention or accounting defect ends attribution without choosing an optimization. A valid study may retain at most one largest clearly identifiable non-callback repeated-work hypothesis with a concrete same-input reuse or equivalent-computation explanation that preserves authentication and failure behavior. A bucket below 10% of the measured non-callback path is not the primary C target for this study. Compare a non-overlapping removable upper bound with the roughly 42% conditional C requirement; removing the entire bucket is only an impossible ceiling, not an achievable saving. Callback ideas retain their separate conditional 12.39% target.

If no defensible hotspot survives, record attribution inconclusive/no selected optimization. Do not expand the workload or rerun unchanged timing. A later investigation of excluded large-history/selection/I/O effects needs evidence supporting that scope. Any candidate requires its own bounded exactness and complete-path qualification before a separately accepted fresh historical invocation.

Use one implementing agent, one distinct static/actual numerical reviewer and the root's independent resource, ownership and temporal review. Reuse valid prior unit and full-inference evidence; do not build a new generalized receipt system or repeat unrelated tests. The profile does not establish historical capacity, enhanced-Elo predictive improvement, external 5% superiority, prospective confirmation or product readiness. Public scope stays front-page Beta/date only.
